 "final_passage": "On the Tamsin-News test split, Verisum achieved a hallucination rate of 8.7%, compared with 11.0% for Corran-Sum with salience pre-filtering and 15.1% for Corran-Sum alone. The relative reduction from Corran-Sum to Verisum (42%) was larger than that from Corran-Sum to Corran-Sum with salience pre-filtering (27%) in this evaluation, though no statistical test was reported and each system was run once. The 27% relative reduction from salience pre-filtering here is similar to the 31% average reduction reported by Varga & Sandoval (2021), although the absolute hallucination rates differ (11.0% vs. 9.8% on average) across different datasets and implementations. ROUGE-L for Verisum (38.9) was slightly higher than for Corran-Sum (38.2) and Corran-Sum with salience pre-filtering (38.0), but these differences are small and no significance test was reported.",
